WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.600
The dog bite admissions rose 81% by 2017, sending more people to hospital after Britain banned

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:13.820
four breeds. This is Unintended Consequences, episode 158. Parliament answered a cluster of

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:19.660
attacks with a breed ban. Police enforced it by looks, owners moved to legal substitutes,

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:25.580
injuries kept climbing, and the statute stayed. In 2018, the House of Commons Environment,

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:32.040
food and rural affairs committee, the EFRA Committee, examined hospital records. Admissions

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:43.000
for dog bites had climbed from 4,110 in 2005 to 7,461 in 2017. The 1991 Dangerous Dogs Act

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:47.960
had banned four types outright and placed strict controls on any others thought to be fighting

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:53.760
dogs. The measure was written to remove dangerous animals from British streets. Instead, the stock

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:58.620
of powerful dogs simply changed shape. To see why that happened, you have to stand where

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:04.200
ministers stood in the spring of 1991. The act was drafted after a cluster of serious

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:10.320
attacks. Several of those attacks involved American pit bull terriers. The cluster prompted urgent

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:15.460
calls for action and parliament. Ministers faced public pressure to act quickly on what appeared

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:21.700
to be a new and identifiable threat. That pressure was not abstract. People had been hurt. Families

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:27.560
were frightened. The dogs in the worst cases seemed to share a look. Ministers chose breed-specific

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:32.940
prohibitions for two reasons that made sense with the information in front of them. The dogs involved

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:38.320
in the worst incidents shared visible physical traits, and similar laws already existed in parts

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:43.880
of the United States. The four types named were the Pitbull Terrier Type, the Japanese Tosa,

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:49.920
the Dogo Argentino, and the Fila Brazillero. Those four were seen as the core of the problem,

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:54.620
them. An exemption register was added so that existing, well-managed dogs could stay

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:59.660
with their owners. The conditions were muscling, insurance, and neutering. At the moment

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:04.360
of passage, the policy looked like a targeted, evidence-based response to a narrow set

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:09.880
of animals. It did not look like a broad attack on all large dogs. The arithmetic seemed

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:14.840
straightforward. Remove the animals whose appearance matched the recent fatalities, and

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:16.180
The risk would fall in proportion.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:22.080
Officials could point to physical markers, broad skulls, muscular frames, short coats.

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:26.220
Those markers distinguished the four listed types from other large breeds.

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:31.380
Because the markers were observable on the street, enforcement could begin without waiting

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:34.120
for behavioral records that many owners did not keep.

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:36.320
That practical point mattered.

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:41.420
A law that needed a paper trail of how every dog had been housed would have been slow to start.

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:45.780
A law that a constable could apply by looking at a dog could start at once.

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:51.180
The exemption scheme softened the measure further, owners who could demonstrate responsible

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:54.260
management could retain their dogs under a formal register.

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:59.420
The design tried to avoid the charge that every animal of a given appearance would be seized

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:00.560
regardless of history.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:02.940
Put yourself in that room for a moment.

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:04.720
Fatalities have clustered.

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:06.960
The public wants a visible answer.

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:10.400
The animals in the worst cases share a set of traits you can see.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:15.220
other jurisdictions have already drawn a line around those traits. A register

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:20.080
lets careful owners keep the dogs they already have under rules. From that

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:25.800
seat, naming four types does not look crude. It looks precise. Royal Ascent came in

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:31.920
August 1991. Police forces began seizing dogs that matched the band types. Courts

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:36.320
applied a deeming process. The bird and sat on owners to prove their animal was

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:41.820
not of a prohibited type. Early enforcement produced visible results. Many pit bull type

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:46.580
dogs were removed from the streets of London and other cities. Government statements at the

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:51.620
time described the register as a practical compromise. The compromise was meant to balance

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:56.860
public safety with the rights of responsible owners. For a while, the street picture matched the

00:03:56.860 --> 00:04:02.100
intention. Dogs that fit the ban description were coming off the pavement. The register was

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:07.220
there for the animals that stayed. Within a few years, veterinary and legal observers began

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:12.160
noting something else. The legal definition of type was difficult to apply consistently

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:17.960
in court. The Deeming Clause required owners to produce expert testimony. That testimony

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:23.280
covered skull measurements, ear set, and tail carriage. Those details could vary between

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:28.200
individual dogs of the same lineage. Courts therefore spent time weighing photographs

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:34.580
and veterinary reports. Courts were not spending that time examining how the animal was housed or exercised.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:38.460
Proponents pointed to the declining number of registered pit bull types.

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:43.260
To those proponents, the decline was proof that the visible threat had been curtailed.

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:49.260
Critics noted that the same physical traits could appear in crosses that fell outside the statutory definitions.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:52.040
Both observations could be true at once.

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:55.260
The listed types were becoming rarer on the register.

00:04:55.260 --> 00:05:00.640
animal that looked powerful and that shared pieces of the same build could still be legal

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:06.320
if they did not meet the type tests. The fight in court was about classification. An owner

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:11.340
might bring a dog in and be told to prove a negative. Prove this animal is not of a prohibited

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:17.340
type. The proof lived in millimeters of skull in how the ears sat and how the tail was carried.

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:22.960
A veterinary report could settle a case without anyone asking how the dog was acquired or who

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:25.460
who walked it, or whether it had been trained for status.

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:29.100
That was not a failure of effort by the people applying the law.

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:31.720
It was what the statute asked them to decide.

00:05:32.340 --> 00:05:38.040
The Royal Society for the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals, the RSPCA, later reviewed 30

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:40.400
fatal dog attacks that occurred after the act.

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:44.560
21 of those 30 involved dogs that were never on the prohibited list.

00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:49.940
The dogs in that majority were mainly Staffordshire bull terrier crosses and mastiff mixes.

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:55.840
Hospital data collected by the 2018 EFRA Committee showed the upward trend in bite injuries

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:57.460
continued without interruption.

00:05:58.220 --> 00:06:02.800
Owners who wanted a dog for status or protection simply turned to breeds that remained legal.

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:07.980
Most often those were Staffordshire bull terrier crosses and other massive type mixes.

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:13.940
These dogs were not subject to the musling or registration rules, yet many possessed comparable

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:15.220
strength and bite force.

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:20.600
Because the law focused on appearance rather than behavior or owner history, enforcement

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:26.020
resources stayed tied up in court cases about ear shape and skull measurements. Those resources

00:06:26.020 --> 00:06:31.920
were not spent assessing how dogs were actually kept. A 1996 perspective study in the journal

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:37.120
injury found no measurable drop in accident and emergency attendances for dog bites after

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:42.680
the act took effect. That finding sits early in the life of the law. The visible removals

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:47.280
in London and other cities had not shown up as fewer people arriving at emergency departments

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:47.920
with bites.

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:52.200
Over time, the visible population of dogs called dangerous shifted.

00:06:52.940 --> 00:06:54.720
The underlying pattern remained intact.

00:06:55.520 --> 00:06:58.660
Powerful animals stayed in the hands of some irresponsible owners.

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:05.560
The veterinary record analysis of cases from 1992 to 2019 confirmed that prohibited types

00:07:05.560 --> 00:07:08.500
continued to appear on the index of exempted dogs.

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:11.080
The ban had not eliminated the animals.

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:16.400
models. The ban had recategorized them. Some dogs of the name types remained, legally

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:22.120
under the register, muzzled and neutered and insured. Others of similar capacity never

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:26.460
entered that system at all because their papers and their measurements kept them outside

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:31.800
the four types. One objection sometimes raised is that the rise in admissions might reflect

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:37.380
better reporting rather than more incidents. The EFRA Committee examined the same data set

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:42.760
across multiple years. The increase persisted even after adjustments for population growth

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:48.460
and changes in hospital coding. Another objection is that the banned breeds were simply replaced by

00:07:48.460 --> 00:07:53.740
animals of similar temperament. The data instead showed that the replacement breeds were chosen

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:58.920
precisely because they escaped the legal definition, not because they lacked physical capacity.

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:05.580
That distinction matters. This was not a mystery of dogs quietly changing character. It was a choice

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:08.820
available to anyone who wanted the capacity without the controls.

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:14.920
The causal chain runs in a straight line, a rule keyed to appearance, owners selecting

00:08:14.920 --> 00:08:20.300
unregulated but equally capable substitutes, a sustained or rising rate of injury that

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:22.320
the original prohibitions could not address.

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:26.280
Walk that chain from the owner's side without sneering at anyone.

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:31.700
If you want a dog that looks imposing or that you believe will protect you, the act tells

00:08:31.700 --> 00:08:34.780
you which looks will bring police, muzzles, and a court fight.

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:37.860
It does not tell you that strength itself is the problem.

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:43.080
A Staffordshire bull terrier cross can clear the statutory tests and still be a powerful

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:43.520
animal.

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:46.080
A massive type mix can do the same.

00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:48.100
No muscling rule attaches.

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:50.320
No register entry is required.

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:54.180
No neutering condition follows from the 1991 list.

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:59.400
The person who would have been a careless owner of a band type can be a careless owner of

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:00.100
a legal type.

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:03.260
The person who wanted status can still buy status.

00:09:03.260 --> 00:09:08.280
The law has changed the name on the paperwork more reliably than it has changed the keeping.

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:10.960
Now walk it from the enforcement side.

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:14.140
A constable in a court can do what the statute defines.

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:16.120
Match the dog to a type.

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:17.600
Argue ear set.

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:19.360
Commission a skull measurement.

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:23.100
Place the burden on the owner to prove the animal is not prohibited.

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:25.060
That work is real work.

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:28.440
It takes police time and expert time and court time.

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:33.820
None of it, by itself, asks whether this owner has a history of letting a dog run at people,

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:38.160
or of keeping a powerful animal in conditions that make a bite more likely.

00:09:38.900 --> 00:09:43.640
Housing and exercise were not the questions the deeming clause was built to answer, so

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:45.880
the second order effect is a misallocation.

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:50.380
The third order effect is substitution that the misallocation cannot see.

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:57.020
Fatal attacks after the act in the RSPCA review mostly involve dogs the list never named.

00:09:57.020 --> 00:10:02.240
Emergency attendances in the 1996 study did not measureably fall.

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:07.640
Hospital admissions in the records the EFRA committee read kept climbing across the

00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:12.100
years the committee checked, including after the committee adjusted for population and

00:10:12.100 --> 00:10:13.920
for how hospitals coded the injuries.

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:20.860
The 2018 EFRA report concluded there was no evidence that breed-specific legislation had reduced

00:10:20.860 --> 00:10:21.500
bite rates.

00:10:21.500 --> 00:10:26.980
The report recommended a move toward deed not breed approaches focused on owner behavior.

00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:29.940
That recommendation is a redesign on paper.

00:10:30.500 --> 00:10:34.220
It says, judge what was done, not which name the dog carries.

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:38.440
Successive governments have kept the 1991 framework in place.

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:40.460
They have added limited amendments.

00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:44.940
One of those amendments extended controls to private property in 2014.

00:10:45.760 --> 00:10:47.740
The core list and the core method remained.

00:10:47.740 --> 00:10:52.840
calls for full repeal continue from veterinary bodies and welfare organizations.

00:10:53.260 --> 00:10:58.520
Yet no replacement system has been enacted. The index of exempted dogs still operates.

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:04.540
Police time continues to be spent on identification disputes rather than preventive work with owners.

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:09.860
The result is a statute that is both retained and widely regarded as ineffective

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:12.360
by the very committees that have studied its outcomes.

00:11:12.360 --> 00:11:15.120
That is a particular kind of stuckness.

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:19.920
The people asked to review the law have said the breed-specific approach does not show

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:21.160
a reduction in bite rates.

00:11:21.940 --> 00:11:26.760
The machinery those reviews inherit is still the machinery of type, deeming, and the index.

00:11:27.460 --> 00:11:31.540
Later reviews have therefore inherited the same enforcement machinery while acknowledging

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:35.960
that the machinery does not track the risk factors that actually produce serious bites.

00:11:36.720 --> 00:11:41.780
Extending controls on to private property in 2014 widened where the existing rules could

00:11:41.780 --> 00:11:47.520
reach. It did not change what those rules measured. A dispute about whether a dog is a prohibited

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:53.740
type can now arise in more places. It is still a dispute about type. Owners of exempted dogs

00:11:53.740 --> 00:11:59.660
remain under muscling, insurance, and neutering rules. Owners of powerful legal substitutes do not

00:11:59.660 --> 00:12:05.260
enter that bargain, because their dogs were never on the list. The register continues to prove that

00:12:05.260 --> 00:12:08.700
some prohibited animals were recategorized rather than removed.

00:12:09.320 --> 00:12:15.920
The veterinary record span from 1992 through 2019 is long enough to show that recategorizing

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:18.360
did not fade as a footnote of the early years.

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:21.080
Prohibited types kept appearing on the index.

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:26.320
Meanwhile, the injuries the Act was written to prevent did not recede in the hospital figures

00:12:26.320 --> 00:12:28.400
the EFRA Committee put on the record.

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:34.500
Empathy for the 1991 decision does not require pretending the later record is ambiguous on the

00:12:34.500 --> 00:12:39.780
central claim. Ministers reached for markers they could see under pressure, with American

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:45.160
precedents in view, and with an exemption meant to spare well-managed dogs. Committees

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:49.820
that came back to the same statute, with admissions data and fatal attack reviews in

00:12:49.820 --> 00:12:55.260
hand, did not find evidence that the prohibitions had reduced bite rates. The fix that was

00:12:55.260 --> 00:13:00.680
available inside the old frame, limited amendment rather than a new system, left the measurement

00:13:00.680 --> 00:13:06.740
problem where it was. When the 1991 Act tied enforcement to visible breed rather than to how an

00:13:06.740 --> 00:13:12.520
individual dog was acquired and kept, it rewarded owners who simply chose unregulated but equally

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:18.660
capable animals. The reward was quiet. Stay off the list, and the musling, the insurance condition,

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:24.340
and the neutering rule that attached to the ban types did not attach to you. Strength could travel

00:13:24.340 --> 00:13:30.080
with the dog. The legal burden did not. When the exemption scheme required owners to prove a negative

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:35.460
in court, it concentrated legal effort on appearance disputes instead of risk assessment.

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:40.360
Skull measurements, ear set, and tail carriage became the contested facts.

00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:45.880
Housing, exercise, and owner history stayed outside the question the Deeming Clause was

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:46.660
written to settle.

00:13:47.420 --> 00:13:52.360
When later reviews documented rising bite numbers yet left the original structure untouched,

00:13:52.880 --> 00:13:54.920
the policy became self-perpetuating.

00:13:54.920 --> 00:14:01.640
The EFRA committee could recommend deed overbreed, veterinary bodies, and welfare organizations

00:14:01.640 --> 00:14:03.360
could keep calling for repeal.

00:14:03.760 --> 00:14:08.600
Without a replacement system, identification disputes remain the work the statute knows

00:14:08.600 --> 00:14:09.400
how to assign.

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:15.460
If you follow regulatory design on environmental intelligence, this is the same mismatch.

00:14:15.980 --> 00:14:20.180
A visible category asked to stand in for the conduct that actually produces harm.

00:14:20.180 --> 00:14:29.940
The same dynamic shows up whenever a rule names a product, a device, or a breed, and a near equivalent stays legal because it fails the naming test.

00:14:30.580 --> 00:14:35.400
Watch what gets counted in the enforcement file, not what the press release says the rule is for.

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:43.680
What single behavior or ownership factor would you measure today if the goal were to reduce serious incidents rather than to name particular breeds?

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:45.660
We'll leave it there for today.

00:14:45.660 --> 00:14:48.040
Thanks for thinking through this one with me.

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:52.820
If you know someone who loves a good cautionary tale, send it their way and I'll see you

